+**Refills from LPDDR** (4.17.13) are requests instead of runs: the loop adds the request's tag to both masks' settings, issues the request and carries on; the tag's event, consumed by the loop's next load, proves the data is in the queue (6.7). At most one LPDDR read is outstanding per queue (6.7).
+
+**Between passes.** The loop exits only at the top, after its last refill run has landed (counters done consumed). Before the next start, the controller also waits for the tag event of every LPDDR read it issued into a queue, so every queue push has landed when the start empties the queues (4.17.8).
 
